# --------------------------------------------------
# Git commit message template.
#
# This file serves as a template for writing consistent commit messages
# that satisfy the Conventional Commits specification.
#
# The recommended setup path configures this template automatically:
# mise run setup
#
# To configure only the commit template without running repository setup, use:
# git config --local commit.template .gitmessage
#
# To create a commit through the interactive prompt, use the developer-facing
# command `mise run commit`, or run the underlying package script directly with
# `pnpm run commit`.
#
# format:           type(scope)!: subject
# header:           complete first line; warns when longer than 72 characters
# subject:          imperative, lowercase start, all caps forbidden, no period;
#                   warns when longer than 50 characters
# type (required):  feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build,
#                   ci, chore, revert
# scope (optional): any non-empty kebab-case value
# dependencies:     use the deps or dev-deps scope as applicable
# body/footer:      separate each from the preceding content with a blank line;
#                   warns when a line is longer than 100 characters
# breaking change:  add ! before the colon and a BREAKING CHANGE footer
# --------------------------------------------------

chore: describe the change

# why: what problem does this solve?
# what: what changed

# BREAKING CHANGE: describe the change and required migration
# Refs: #issue
